        "# Results\n",
        "\n",
        "Using 8 matches provided a better outcome than using 10 or 20 matches. Using more matches leads to including matches that confuse the model. We use RANSAC to reject the inconsistent matches which improves the performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "The images show this story. The number of matches increase as you look down. From left to right, we have our matches in the first image, the least squares fit, then the RANSAC fit. The red overlay is the transformed source image. With RANSAC, the red overlay represents the box's actualy position and shape much more closely."
